  "message": "I checked with agent_creator: Now let's smoke-test it.--help works. Now a real dry-run against the actual lance_data to prove it executes end to end without mutating anything.Now let's create the agent folder structure.No `tools/` declarations needed (no declared capability beyond the ADW itself — leaving the folder empty reports as a stub, which is accurate). Now let's register the agent: extra_roles.py, roles.py, and Toyota's system prompt.Now let's make the three edits.Now Toyota's system prompt — add a ROUTE example.I'll add a new section before \"ORDINARY CONVERSATION\".Now run the full verification gate.Everything passes — the gate is clean, no reverts needed. All done.\n\nI built memory_compactor, a delegated specialist that prunes conversation turns older than a retention window out of the shared LanceDB memory store and then reclaims the freed space, refusing on its own rather than let a cutoff clear a whole table. It drives a new ADW, adw_memory_compact.py (survey, purge, compact phases, all code, no agent needed), which I smoke-tested both in a dry run that correctly previewed removals and in a run that correctly refused to empty a table. The agent is registered in extra_roles.py, roles.py, and Toyota's system prompt, and the full verification gate, including every receptionist_team test, passed; Toyota will pick it up on her next restart.",
